<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Buyan-Badyrgy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1932</span> · Also known as Mongush Buyan-Badyrgy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Buyan-Badyrgy was a Tuvan noble and politician who led the government of the Tuvan People's Republic in the 1920s. He favoured a moderate course that respected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a> and the traditional order and sought closer ties with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a>. The Soviet authorities, who wanted a firmer communist line, had him removed in the late 1920s, and he was later arrested and executed in 1932.</p></div>
